<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dexippus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 210–273</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Publius Herennius Dexippus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dexippus was an Athenian statesman and historian of the 3rd century. He is said to have led the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> against the Heruli in 267, and he wrote a chronicle of world history and the Scythica, an account of the Gothic wars. These survive only in fragments, including his record of the Juthungi envoys' negotiations with Emperor Aurelian.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dexippus.jpg" alt="Dexippus" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Furius · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I.Eleusis_656_%3D_IG_II%C2%B2_3671(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
